<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA IAIFO REPORTS PROFIT AFTER LOSS.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA IAIFO REPORTS PROFIT AFTER LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (billion of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit				 71.6 million vs  loss 12.04</p>
<p> Turnover				  77.45     vs    48.59</p>
<p> Fixed assets			   103.12     vs    96.09</p>
<p> Current assets			  52.77     vs    37.77</p>
<p> Total assets			   161.01     vs   135.29</p>
<p> Share capital			   92.58     vs    92.58</p>
<p> Total debts			     75.04     vs    54.27</p>
<p> Total dividends			  nil	vs    n.a.</p>
<p>NOTE -- IAIFO is a state-run industrial fittings manufacturer listed on the second tier of the Bucharest stock exchange. Data, reported to the bourse, are in nominal terms and in line with Romanian accounting standards. The company report said its 1996 profit would go to the development fund and would also cover losses in previous years. ($=7,084 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
